course: dictionary
lesson: 6500
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word neck can name a body part, the top of a bottle, or the part of a jumper that goes round your neck. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings by the neck, beak or legs.» Here the neck is a body part, because beaks and legs are body parts too.
explain: Look for clues in the rest of the sentence. «Ostriches lie flat with their necks along the ground.» Ostriches are animals with bodies, so their necks are body parts that can lie along the ground.
explain: Some words are used in special phrases, and these do not mean what each word means alone. «Neck and neck» means two runners are exactly level, and «a pain in the neck» means an annoying person or job. If a phrase sounds silly when you take it word by word, it is probably an idiom.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: The neck is the part of the body that joins the head to the shoulders, and it lets the head turn.
fact: The neck of a bottle or a guitar is its long, thin top part.
fact: «Neck and neck» means exactly level, as in two runners in a race.
fact: Never put cords or ropes round your neck, because a neck injury is serious.
exercise: «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings by the neck, beak or legs.» In this sentence, what is the neck? | The top of a bottle | The part of a jumper that goes round your neck | *A part of the body that joins the head to the shoulders | A type of rope
exercise: «The neck of the guitar was long and thin.» What does neck mean here? | The collar of a shirt | *The long, thin top part of an instrument | A short piece of string | A part of the body
exercise: Which word is the plural of neck? | necked | nicks | neckers | *necks
test: «Ruby and Sam were neck and neck at the end of the race.» What does neck and neck mean? | *Exactly level | Stuck together | Lost in the crowd | Far behind the others
test: Why should you never put a cord or rope round your neck? | *It can cause a serious injury, so keep cords away from your neck | It can cause a serious injury | It makes you taller | It keeps you warm
exam: «Mum said my little brother is a pain in the neck.» What does a pain in the neck mean? | A serious injury | *An annoying person or job | A sore part of the body after sport | A long, thin top part
